      {
        "file": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r99/discovery.md",
        "sha256": "28ceab4402ec69f637f8ef4eadde3f59ad3c02fea0aa414d099cf50e54f66e73",
        "lines": [
          "* Alikhani\u2013Ghanbari, arXiv2607.22686v1, actual HTML: definitions2.1\u20132.3 and final problems7.1\u20137.3. These concern super coalition partitions, a different invariant. A separate secondary lead to their submitted *Super domatic in graphs* was not promoted: no actual primary body or literal partition-count conjecture was obtained. No Q3-based nomination is made from that lead."
        ]
      },
      {
        "file": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r99/sources/coalition.txt",
        "sha256": "683f871fb1bfa3e1eb69197eb5b943f80bb8404d0e5b6de5cce4e8ba7544caa6",
        "lines": [
          " Saeid Alikhani",
          " \u00a0\u00a0alikhani@yazd.ac.ir, n.ghanbari.math@gmail.com ",
          " Following this seminal work, coalition parameters have been generalized and examined across multiple structural domains. Alikhani et al.\u00a0 [ 2 ]  explored total coalitions in graphs, where the combined sets must form a total dominating set, ensuring that every vertex in the graph possesses a neighbor within the dominating coalition. In 2025, Alikhani, Bakhshesh, Golmohammadi, and Klav\u017ear\u00a0 [ 3 ]  introduced independent coalitions, imposing the constraint that the partnering sets or the resulting coalition must maintain an independent internal structure, which introduces profound challenges regarding independent partitioning. Concurrently, the study of connected coalitions\u00a0 [ 4 ]  demanded that the induced subgraph of the union must be connected, reflecting practical demands in communication systems where tracking sensors must remain continually linked to pass information securely. ",
          "  S. Alikhani, D. Bakhshesh, H. Golmohammadi, Total coalitions in graphs,  Quaest. Math.  (2024)  47 (11) 2283-2294. https://doi.org/10.2989/16073606.2024.2365365",
          "  S. Alikhani, D. Bakhshesh, H. Golmohammadi, S. Klav\u017ear, On independent coalition in graphs and independent coalition graphs,  Discuss. Math. Graph Theory,  45 (2025) 533\u2013544. https://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2543",
          "  S. Alikhani, D. Bakhshesh, H. Golmohammadi, E.V. Konstantinova, Connected coalitions in graphs,  Discuss. Math. Graph Theory   44  (2024) 1551\u20131566. https://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2509",
          "  S. Alikhani, N. Ghanbari, Super domatic in graphs, submitted."
        ]
      },
